sted CI cache activation and harden acceptance evidence\n\nIntroduced by: PR #80 cache/observation work exposed host-environment gaps;\nthe shell-dependent legacy logcat normalization fixture predates this PR.\nUse case: Passing builds must actually exercise cache reuse, and validation\nmust distinguish incomplete evidence and fixture timing from correct behavior.\n\nThe first PR run inherited a real GITHUB_SHA into a synthetic observation\nfixture, while native Windows uppercased VS/SDK environment names before a\ncase-sensitive dictionary lookup. Local fixtures did not model those inputs.\nIsolate observation identities and normalize Windows lookup keys without\nchanging serialized identities, required fields or configuration isolation.\n\nRestore Linux's established mtime compiler-check policy inside unchanged,\ndigest-qualified images. A real seeded-cache test proves that the content\npolicy transition alone invalidates objects; restore-only PRs could not replace\nthose shared seeds. Keep content checking for native macOS runner variation.\n\nMake the legacy-error unit fixture deterministic through the existing process\nseam, retain real stderr-file/notification behavior and real-child smoke, and\nrequire observed completion with useful diagnostics. The precise old CI startup\nerror was not recorded; this is not claimed as a production sanitizer fix.\n\nReject malformed/incomplete performance evidence, exercise the consumer's real\nreceipt bindings, and hard-disable destructive cache cleanup until the missing\napproval environment is configured and a reviewed activation removes the\ninterlock. Preserve the failed first PR run's actual metrics without relabeling\nit as warm or successful acceptance evidence.\n\nVerification: targeted observation, ccache, Windows cache, report, cleanup and\nlock suites passed. Exact modified transport tests passed on Intel Xcode 26.6,\nQt 5.15.18 and Qt 6.9.3 with ASan+UBSan and QT_NO_KEYWORDS (44 assertions each).\nReal cache invalidation and hostile Actions-environment regressions went from\nRED to GREEN. Full batched quality validation will run before push; hosted\nactivation/warm acceptance still requires the next CI run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:03:00Z","author":{"name":"ZEACENT","email":"zeacent@qq.com"},"committer":{"name":"ZEACENT","email":"zeacent@qq.com"}},"repository":{"id":1094649085,"node_id":"R_kgDOQT8E_Q","name":"klogg","full_name":"ZEACENT/klogg","private":false,"owner":{"login":"ZEACENT","id":46587442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTg3NDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46587442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT","html_url":"https://github.com/ZEACENT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZEACENT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/ZEACENT/klogg","description":"Really fast log explorer based on glogg project","fork":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZEACENT/klogg","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZEACENT/klogg/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZEACENT/klogg/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZEACENT/klogg/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZEACENT/klogg/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZEACENT/klogg/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://a